// the weight fetch changed: weights are int8 [M, K] row-major with one FP32 scale
// per output row; activations stay BF16 [N, K]; output BF16 [N, M].
//   * same persistent work-groups (grid = CuCount, block = THRDS x WvPrGrp),
//     LDS-staged activations with global fallback past the LDS capacity,
//     row_shr DPP + xor-16 lane reduction, FP32 accumulation in the same
//     pairwise form as the gfx1x bf16 DOT2C;
//   * each lane loads 16 int8 weights per 16-byte non-temporal load, converts
//     them exactly to FP32, and the per-row scale is applied once before the
//     BF16 store (exact INT8 math: sum_k x_k * q_k, then * scale).
#include <torch/all.h>
#include <torch/extension.h>
#include <ATen/hip/HIPContext.h>
